  "method": [
    "Use the exact cereal Cap’n Proto schema of each of two logged openpilot revisions; read and check initData gitCommit and WheeledBody config for every segment. Count carParams with COMMA BODY where present.",
    "The pinned carcontroller maps incoming actuators.accel/5 and -steer/2 to desired speed and speed difference, combines PID outputs, applies a deadband offset, limits internal per-update change to ±50 and clips each final wheel command to ±500. This branch requires CC.enabled and valid orientation and angular velocity; otherwise it emits zero. It writes final left/right integers to actuatorsOutput.accel/.steer and duplicates right in steerOutputCan. Upstream desired speed/turn fields do not provide pre-limit torque.",
    "Parse 0x250 (592) in sendcan src=0 versus can src=128; 16-bit big-endian signed left and right values followed by two payload bytes including rolling counter and checksum. Use received 0x201 (513) src=0 signed left/right wheel speed and 0x204 (516) src=0 four signed raw phase channels. DBC specifies no unit for torque or phase fields. Wheel speed is treated as native wheel-rate counts, used as RPM in the controller conversion with SPEED_FROM_RPM=0.008587.",
    "For each sent frame, find the nearest report or echo by logMonoTime, at most 10 ms in either direction. Prefer earlier candidates at equal distances. Count nearest identical left/right pair and, for CAN echo, byte-identical full six-byte payload. Separately search all candidates within ±10 ms and [0,20] ms using the wheel pair for reports or entire payload for echoes. Count ambiguous and unique matches, and, among queries with exactly one candidate, count those not sharing it with another singly matched query. Counts use sent frames as denominator.",
    "For each wheel separately, label sent-command slots at |value|=500 or inside that bound. Use nearest host-event wheel-speed or phase-current frame within ±10 ms. Report distinct selected frames and matched sample counts, sums, sum of squares and extrema. Zero observations have blank extrema and median timing distance. The table has 69 segments × 2 wheels × 2 regimes × 3 channels.",
    "Check consecutive command differences only within each segment; count exact jumps of absolute size 50 and over 50. Different segment boundaries, recording gaps, enable-state changes and absent pre-limit values limit interpretation. In the separate command-step table, restrict pairs to host stamps 5–15 ms apart and relate exact absolute increments (0, 1–49, 50, >50) to independently logged speed/phase channels within ±10 ms of the second send. The side-specific 50-count groups are observable comparisons even when no 500-count amplitude rails occur."
  ],
